<title>FRANCE: Smaller loss at France's GIAT - union sources.</title>
<headline>Smaller loss at France's GIAT - union sources.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>GIAT Industries, France's tank and munition producer, made a 1996 operating loss of 1.3 billion francs against 1.6 billion in 1995, labour union sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>There was no immediate comment at GIAT. A board meeting is taking place this morning.</p>
<p>In 1995, GIAT posted a net loss of 10 billion francs due to heavy provisions.</p>
</text>
